{"id": "EUVD-2026-86654", "enisaUuid": "ed68b5f8-d3d3-3ddd-bc94-b16d311156ca", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhwmon: (ltc4282) Make sure clk_init_data is fully initialized\n\nThe clk_init_data structure contains several mutually-exclusive members\nfor different methods to specify the possible parents of a clock,\nprompting drivers to initialize only the members they need.  However,\nnot initializing all members may cause subtle issues, which are only\nexposed when CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_PATTERN or CONFIG_INIT_STACK_NONE is\nenabled.\n\nltc428_clk_provider_setup() does not fill in any parent clocks, and\nassumes that init.num_parents is NULL.  However, the latter in\nuninitialized, and thus may cause a crash.\n\nMake sure all members are fully initialized, to fix such bugs, and to\navoid future breakage when converting drivers to a different method for\nspecifying the parents.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4a96da5a3f132d80aa971ddbeb86808539ba0e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80b46a3d066d4e2c1dd4edb90d4aa3f22ca79f39", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa08ce1ffaf36c7bdd3edd0ad65f72413639bfad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e317326d1755ea054b98e7a4833b929157461c35"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98001", "GHSA-p8xj-pv98-49jm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "29d65f6b-5c65-3083-8847-a29cf3adf287", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "3b81196d-3c44-336b-839f-b2e0649331fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cbc29538dbf7d7400f1ffc5dd5713e6a551463a0 <80b46a3d066d4e2c1dd4edb90d4aa3f22ca79f39"}, {"id": "501bb888-c07b-3d04-9529-2d101a68af3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "5c581c88-d665-3df6-a969-6f2074889252", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "8c595695-7594-3e69-a263-ddd453d4dda5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cbc29538dbf7d7400f1ffc5dd5713e6a551463a0 <c4a96da5a3f132d80aa971ddbeb86808539ba0e6"}, {"id": "95f8e0af-32d3-36dc-9449-2a3db6f4968b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a6d12f9b-f340-389a-b631-49e02d271570", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d19fa25f-9e8f-35df-9d92-9a3e0e82618c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "f12f8224-ee68-3a0a-b573-d4c068183ba2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cbc29538dbf7d7400f1ffc5dd5713e6a551463a0 <aa08ce1ffaf36c7bdd3edd0ad65f72413639bfad"}, {"id": "f3b8d9c3-2800-37d5-a1bd-1fd5de19a2bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cbc29538dbf7d7400f1ffc5dd5713e6a551463a0 <e317326d1755ea054b98e7a4833b929157461c35"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "88e8e9e9-87fa-324e-8669-b9237476463b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}